          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शापः (śāpaḥ) comes from the root √śap, \"to curse\", as in śapati; MW gives śāpa as a curse, malediction, oath (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
